From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Paul <vipoll@mainlining.org>
Subject: [PATCH 18/19] FROMLIST: usb: typec: fsa4480: Add chip id read retry
 loop

The first read attempt may fail on some devices (e.g. Xiaomi Pad 6), which
makes the FSA4480 SBU mux probe fail with:

  fsa4480 15-0042: error -ENODEV: FSA4480 not found

Because the PMIC Type-C block (pm8150b_typec) consumes this mux, the whole
USB-C stack then stays in deferred probe and DisplayPort altmode never comes
up.  Retry the device id read a few times before giving up.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260511122246.31673-1-vipoll@mainlining.org/
Signed-off-by: Victor Paul <vipoll@mainlining.org>
---
 drivers/usb/typec/mux/fsa4480.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/mux/fsa4480.c b/drivers/usb/typec/mux/fsa4480.c
index c54e42c7e6a1..ae496c0fa805 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/mux/fsa4480.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/mux/fsa4480.c
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/bits.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/i2c.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
@@ -256,6 +257,7 @@ static int fsa4480_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	struct typec_switch_desc sw_desc = { };
 	struct typec_mux_desc mux_desc = { };
 	struct fsa4480 *fsa;
+	int retries = 5;
 	int val = 0;
 	int ret;
 
@@ -278,7 +280,12 @@ static int fsa4480_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	if (ret && ret != -ENODEV)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "Failed to get regulator\n");
 
-	ret = regmap_read(fsa->regmap, FSA4480_DEVICE_ID, &val);
+	do {
+		ret = regmap_read(fsa->regmap, FSA4480_DEVICE_ID, &val);
+		if (!ret)
+			break;
+		usleep_range(1000, 1200);
+	} while (retries--);
 	if (ret)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, -ENODEV, "FSA4480 not found\n");
 
